CREM attribution: publications based on this program or modified versions should cite https://github.com/pytlotad/CREM-QI and credit Tadeusz Slawomir Pytlos (tadeusz.slawomir.pytlos@gmail.com).
External magnetic field: none.
Charge radiation reaction: individual (reduced-order Landau-Lifshitz per particle).
Trajectory integrator: adaptive symmetric second-order step.
Pair: electron + positron (reduced mass 0.5 m_e, Bohr radius 2 a0, binding 6.80285 eV).
Starting separation: a_n = 1 a_pair (n = 1) = 105.835 pm -- an initial condition for the classical inspiral, not a claimed energy eigenstate.
Preparation: L = (l + 1/2) hbar with n = 1, l = 0 -- the rung the wave lock carries any start to (audits 646-647; CREM_WAVE_LOCK=0 turns the lock off); --circular-start restores L = n hbar.
Running 200 paired final-state annihilations on 4 workers (n = 1, L = 0.5 hbar, spins quantized, photon cascade with the action rule; audit 375).
  --contact-barrier restores the legacy barrier-crossing mechanism (audits 314-320).
final-state pairs: 50/200
final-state pairs: 100/200
final-state pairs: 150/200
final-state pairs: 200/200

Final-state annihilation (statistical experiment 6, audit 375)
  Gamma = sigma v [w + (1-w) eps] n_QR at the final state (the rate of experiments 1/2); t from the engine's survival along the cascade, then Exp(1/Gamma) (audit 379);
  imports: n_QR (Quigga-Rosner), sigma v = 4 pi r_e^2 c, eps = 1/1113.9 (Ore-Powell, LO QED); both rates to order alpha^2 (audit 575): p-Ps x 0.994669, o-Ps x 0.976262

  para : 200 decays (0 failed); final state <L>/hbar 0.5, <w> 1, <cascade> 0.000303966 ps, <survival of the cascade> 0.999998, decayed during the cascade 0/200
         engine 1/Gamma 125.161 ps (1/<Gamma> 125.161 ps)
         tau (MLE = mean t) 116.469 +/- 8.23558 ps, median/ln2 100.857 ps, sd/mean 1.10587 (exponential: 1)
         KS vs Exp(tau): D = 0.0554877, p = 0.557531 (conservative, tau fitted)
         measured 125.142 ps (Al-Ramadhan & Gidley, PRL 72, 1632 (1994)), ratio 0.930692
         t/tau bins: [0,0.5) 87/78.69  [0.5,1.0) 46/47.73  [1,1.5) 21/28.95  [1.5,2.0) 18/17.56  [2,3.0) 13/17.11  [3,4.0) 9/6.294  [4,inf) 6/3.663
  ortho: 200 decays (0 failed); final state <L>/hbar 0.5, <w> 0, <cascade> 3.03966e-07 ns, <survival of the cascade> 1, decayed during the cascade 0/200
         engine 1/Gamma 142.046 ns (1/<Gamma> 142.046 ns)
         tau (MLE = mean t) 139.04 +/- 9.83159 ns, median/ln2 124.224 ns, sd/mean 1.13541 (exponential: 1)
         KS vs Exp(tau): D = 0.0588782, p = 0.480348 (conservative, tau fitted)
         measured 142.037 ns (Vallery et al., PRL 90, 203402 (2003)), ratio 0.978898
         t/tau bins: [0,0.5) 87/78.69  [0.5,1.0) 46/47.73  [1,1.5) 28/28.95  [1.5,2.0) 14/17.56  [2,3.0) 11/17.11  [3,4.0) 6/6.294  [4,inf) 8/3.663

  tau_ortho/tau_para = 1193.79 +/- 10%  (selection rule 1/eps = 1113.9; measured 1135.0 from the two lifetimes above)

  Annihilation photons (rest frame; 2 gamma axis isotropic; 3 gamma plane normal ~ 1 - cos^2/3 about S at contact, audit 320)
  para : 2 gamma 200, 3 gamma 0, <|S1+S2|>/hbar at contact 0
         max |sum k|c/W 0, max |sum E - W|/W 0
  ortho: 2 gamma 0, 3 gamma 200, <|S1+S2|>/hbar at contact 1, <P2(n.S)> -0.0861725 (QED -0.05), <S.(k1 x k2)> -0.00318497 (QED 0)
         max |sum k|c/W 1.1238e-15, max |sum E - W|/W 1.11022e-16
  generator self-test (200000 draws, S = z): <P2> -0.0502263 (exact -0.05, sd 0.001), <S.(k1 x k2)> -0.000255124 (0), <x1> 0.666921 (2/3), max |sum k|c/W 1.67308e-14
